      "content": "Here's an updated draft memo:\n\nSubject: Promoting Ergonomic Workspaces for Your Well-being\n\nDear Remote Team,\n\nAs we continue to work together to drive innovation and success, we want to take a moment to remind you of the importance of maintaining proper ergonomics in your workspace. This includes setting up your desk and workstation to promote good posture, reduce strain on your wrists and back, and prevent discomfort. Over time, small, nagging pains can culminate into more serious issues if left unchecked - strain on muscles and joints can lead to long-term damage and decreased productivity. By taking a few simple precautions, you can avoid these issues altogether.\n\nTo ensure your comfort and well-being, please refer to the following guidelines:\n\n* Monitor height: Position your monitor directly in front of you, at a distance of about 20-25 inches, and at a height that allows you to gaze slightly downward (approximately 4-5 inches below eye level).\n* Sitting posture: Sit with your feet flat on the floor or on a footrest, if needed, to maintain a 90-degree angle between your hips and knees. Keep your back straight, shoulders relaxed, and head level.\n* Keyboard and mouse: Place your keyboard directly in front",
